Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:19:57 +0330
Subject: [PATCH] Input: synaptics - enable SMBus for HP ZBook 17 G3

The touchpad on the HP ZBook 17 G3 (PNP: SYN3040 SYN0100 SYN0002
PNP0f13, board id 2706, fw id 2017334) reports that it supports
InterTouch, and the kernel suggests reporting it:

  psmouse serio3: synaptics: Your touchpad (PNP: SYN3040 SYN0100 SYN0002
  PNP0f13) says it can support a different bus. If i2c-hid and hid-rmi
  are not used, you might want to try setting psmouse.synaptics_intertouch
  to 1 and report this to linux-input@vger.kernel.org.

With psmouse.synaptics_intertouch=1 it binds over SMBus as
"Synaptics TM2706-002" through rmi4_smbus (i2c-i801). Pointer motion,
tapping, the physical buttons, two-finger scrolling and the pointing stick
with its three buttons all work, as they do over PS/2.

Add its PNP ID to smbus_pnp_ids so it uses SMBus by default.

Tested on an HP ZBook 17 G3 (BIOS N81 01.62) with Ubuntu's 7.0.0 kernel and
psmouse.synaptics_intertouch=1. The PNP ID was found and the test was run
with the help of an AI coding assistant (Claude); I verified the result on
the machine.
---
 drivers/input/mouse/synaptics.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/mouse/synaptics.c b/drivers/input/mouse/synaptics.c
index b007e642e..62765222a 100644
--- a/drivers/input/mouse/synaptics.c
+++ b/drivers/input/mouse/synaptics.c
@@ -198,6 +198,7 @@ static const char * const smbus_pnp_ids[] = {
 	"SYN1221", /* TUXEDO InfinityBook Pro 14 v5 */
 	"SYN3003", /* HP EliteBook 850 G1 */
 	"SYN3015", /* HP EliteBook 840 G2 */
+	"SYN3040", /* HP ZBook 17 G3 */
 	"SYN3052", /* HP EliteBook 840 G4 */
 	"SYN3221", /* HP 15-ay000 */
 	"SYN323d", /* HP Spectre X360 13-w013dx */
